From bbbdb7eb1e40f7ad1bc49147955579e1dabdcdeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dr3murr <r3muxd@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:24:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Use the real weapon names for the former mega1..5 slots
 in scripts

Renames every script reference to mp_weapon_mega1..5 (damage source enum
entries in place so the numeric values stay put, damageSourceStrings,
WEAPON_*_NAME consts, item/attachment/mod tables, unlock levels,
challenges, burn card escalation, titan ability and HUD switches, stats,
grunt loadouts, gun game, the charge cannon projectile and the throwing
knife). The engine resolves the damage source by weapon class name, so the
enum keys must match the class names.

Left alone on purpose: mp_weapon_mega6..17 and mp_weapon_mega_turret (stock
semantics), and the commented level.megaMaps table in _base_gametype.nut
(unrelated titan-weapon mapping for the unused mega6..16 slots).

The developer-only precache loop now starts at mega6 because mega1..5 no
longer have weapon definitions.
